      "question": "<strong>Case Study:</strong> A horse is tied to a post by a rope. If the horse moves along a circular path, always keeping the rope tight, and describes 88 meters when it traces an angle of $72^\\circ$ at the center.<br>(i) Find the length of the rope (radius).<br>(ii) If the angle was $36^\\circ$, what would be the arc length?",
      "finalAnswer": "(i) 70m, (ii) 44m",
      "solutionSteps": [
        "(i) $l = 88$ m, $\\theta = 72^\\circ = 72 \\times \\frac{\\pi}{180} = \\frac{2\\pi}{5}$ rad.",
        "$l = r\\theta \\implies 88 = r \\times \\frac{2}{5} \\times \\frac{22}{7}$.",
        "$88 = r \\times \\frac{44}{35} \\implies r = \\frac{88 \\times 35}{44} = 70$ m.",
